{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on an aspiration level defined as the mean of all outcomes in the decision problem, ignoring their probabilities. The outcomes in the problem are 4000, 0 (from Lottery B) and 3000 (from Lottery A). The mean of these outcomes is (4000 + 0 + 3000) / 3 = 2333.33 Euros. This is the aspiration level. The reason then evaluates each lottery by the probability that its outcomes yield a positive difference from this aspiration level (i.e., > 2333.33). For Lottery A: the outcome 3000 > 2333.33, so the difference is positive with 100% probability. For Lottery B: 4000 > 2333.33 (positive, 80%), and 0 < 2333.33 (negative, 20%). So the probability of a positive difference is 80%. Since 100% > 80%, the reason would prefer Lottery A. Thus, the reason can be applied, and it favors Lottery A.",
